# Vault and NIP-07

## Secrets

- Private keys, mnemonics, and decrypted vault material stay in the background service worker / vault handlers only.
- Never send secrets to content scripts, page-world, popup React trees, or `window` globals.
- Lock and auto-lock must clear secrets from memory; do not leave plaintext keys after lock.

## Signing surface

- Expose NIP-07 `window.nostr` only; do not implement WebLN / payments.
- Inject/bridge scripts (`nip07-inject`, `nip07-bridge`) must remain thin message relays — signing happens in the service worker.
- Page↔bridge NIP-07 RPC uses a capability-bound `MessageChannel` (see `page-bridge-protocol.ts`); do not put request/response bodies on public `window.postMessage` after handshake.
- Check host permissions / origin before sign or publish; grant site access intentionally from the popup.
- Enforce kind-aware `signEvent` bounds (`sign-event-bounds.ts`) before queueing or signing — e.g. kind `32009` content ≤ 144 Unicode chars; other kinds use larger finite caps. Require `tags` and `created_at`.
- Activity log is one generic `activityLog` list: method, decision, domain, time; optional `kind` / `eventId` (signed) / `reason` (unsuccessful). Never persist event content/tags. Enforce `ACTIVITY_LOG_GLOBAL_MAX` and serialize writes.

## Keep-alive

- `vault-keepalive` alarms exist to keep the unlocked vault warm — they are not the trust-graph keep-alive design in `docs/architecture.md`.
- Do not conflate vault unlock lifetime with WoT graph residency.

## Changes

- Validate imported keys and user-controlled inputs before persistence.
- Prefer dedicated low-value keys for early testing guidance in UI copy; never log secrets.
- After vault/NIP-07 behavior changes, extend unit tests around handlers and permission checks.
